IMPORT prelude

-- Federal Lands Commissioner, Malaysia (Incorporation) Act 1959 (Singapore) -- the Corporation's seal (s 3(2)), its powers to deal
-- in property (s 4), how its deeds are executed and proved (s 5), proof of the Commissioner's appointment (s 6), what property vests
-- in it (s 7), what rights and liabilities pass to it (s 8), its standing under the Land Acquisition Act 1966 (s 9), and the saving
-- for other people's rights (s 11).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FLCMIA1959.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The Legislative
-- History it carries lists no amending Act after Ordinance 71 of 1959 (Transfer of Powers Ordinance 1959) and G.N. No. S (N.S.)
-- 179/1959, followed by the 1970, 1985 and 2020 Revised Editions. NUMBERING: the Arrangement of Sections at the top of the deposit is
-- one out of step with the body (it puts "Short title" against 2 and "Interpretation" against 3); this encoding follows the BODY,
-- where s 1 is the short title and s 11 the saving.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0233 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The person this Act touches is a counterparty of the Corporation -- a buyer, lessee, mortgagee or
-- litigant dealing with land in Singapore held for the Government of Malaysia -- and the questions it answers are: is this
-- property the Corporation's, did this liability pass to it, is this deed properly executed, and is this person really the
-- Commissioner.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title), s 2 (definitions, used in comments only), s 3(1) (incorporation itself), s 10 (the Act is deemed a
-- private Act for the Registration of Deeds Act 1988 -- a bare deeming with nothing to decide). What s 11 of the Registration of
-- Deeds Act 1988, disapplied by s 5(2), requires was not read: that Act is not in this row's deposit.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Federal Lands Commissioner, Malaysia (Incorporation) Act 1959`

§§ `3(2) -- the corporate seal`

-- s 3(2): the Corporation "may sue and be sued in its name and shall have perpetual succession and a corporate seal ... and, until a
-- seal is provided under this section, a stamp bearing the inscription 'the Federal Lands Commissioner' may be used as the corporate
-- seal."
--
-- Inference (the text does not say it): once a seal has been provided, the stamp may no longer be used as the corporate seal.
GIVEN `used the seal provided` IS A BOOLEAN, `used the inscribed stamp` IS A BOOLEAN, `a seal has been provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the impression counts as the corporate seal` IF
        `used the seal provided` AND `a seal has been provided`
    OR  `used the inscribed stamp` AND (NOT `a seal has been provided`)

§§ `4 -- powers to deal in property`

-- s 4: the Corporation "may enter into contracts and may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of
-- every description, and may convey, assign, surrender and yield up, charge, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer or otherwise
-- dispose of, or deal with, any movable or immovable property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as to the Corporation seem
-- fit."
--
-- The power to acquire is unqualified; the power to dispose reaches only property "vested in the Corporation".
DECLARE Dealing IS ONE OF
    `entering into a contract`
    `buying land`
    `holding land`
    `selling land`
    `mortgaging land`
    `leasing land out`
    `surrendering a lease`
    `transferring movable property`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is a disposition` IF
    CONSIDER `the dealing`
    WHEN `selling land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `mortgaging land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `leasing land out` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `surrendering a lease` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `transferring movable property` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation has power for the dealing` IF
        (NOT `the dealing is a disposition` `the dealing`)
    OR  `the property is vested in the Corporation`

§§ `5 -- execution of deeds`

-- s 5(1): instruments requiring the seal "shall be sealed with the seal of the Corporation in the presence of the Federal Lands
-- Commissioner who shall sign every such deed ... and such signing shall be sufficient evidence that the seal was duly and properly
-- affixed and that the seal is the lawful seal of the Corporation."
-- s 5(2): "Section 11 of the Registration of Deeds Act 1988 shall not apply to any instrument purporting to be executed under
-- subsection (1)."
--
-- The evidential benefit needs both the Commissioner's presence and the Commissioner's signature. The s 5(2) disapplication needs
-- only that the instrument PURPORTS to be executed under s 5(1).
GIVEN `sealed with the corporate seal` IS A BOOLEAN, `sealed in the Commissioner's presence` IS A BOOLEAN, `signed by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is executed under s 5(1)` IF
    `sealed with the corporate seal` AND `sealed in the Commissioner's presence` AND `signed by the Commissioner`

GIVEN `signed by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN, `the seal was affixed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signing is sufficient evidence of due sealing` IF
    `signed by the Commissioner` AND `the seal was affixed`

GIVEN `purports to be executed under s 5(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Registration of Deeds Act s 11 applies to it` IF
    NOT `purports to be executed under s 5(1)`

§§ `6 -- proof of the Commissioner's appointment`

-- s 6: "A notification in the Malaysia Gazette of the appointment of any person to be the Federal Lands Commissioner shall be
-- conclusive evidence that that person was duly so appointed."
-- s 2: the Commissioner is "appointed under the relevant law for the time being in force in Malaysia".
--
-- Only the Malaysia Gazette is named. A notification elsewhere is not made conclusive by s 6 (it may still be evidence of some
-- weight -- the Act does not say).
DECLARE Notice IS ONE OF
    `a notification in the Malaysia Gazette`
    `a notification in the Singapore Government Gazette`
    `a letter of appointment`
    `no notification`

GIVEN `the notice` IS A Notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment is conclusively proved` IF
    CONSIDER `the notice`
    WHEN `a notification in the Malaysia Gazette` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `7 -- what property vests in the Corporation`

-- s 7(1): "All movable and immovable property in Singapore which, immediately before 27 February 1959 was vested in the Chief
-- Secretary, Federation of Malaya, under the provisions of the Chief Secretary, Federation of Malaya (Incorporation) Ordinance (Cap.
-- 294, 1955 Revised Edition), shall, on that date and without any conveyance, assignment or transfer whatever, vest in the
-- Corporation for the like title, estate or interest and on the like tenure".
-- s 7(2): "The President may, by order, vest in the Corporation any property ... for the time being vested in any officer or person
-- for the purposes of the Government of Malaysia and, upon the coming into operation of any such order, the property ... shall,
-- without any conveyance ... vest in the Corporation for the like title, estate or interest and on the like tenure".
-- s 2: "property" includes estates, interests, easements and rights, legal or equitable, and things in action.
GIVEN `in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `vested in the Chief Secretary immediately before 27 February 1959` IS A BOOLEAN, `vested under the 1955 Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property vested on 27 February 1959` IF
    `in Singapore` AND `vested in the Chief Secretary immediately before 27 February 1959` AND `vested under the 1955 Ordinance`

GIVEN `a President's order covers it` IS A BOOLEAN, `held by an officer for the Government of Malaysia` IS A BOOLEAN, `the order is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property vests by President's order` IF
    `a President's order covers it` AND `held by an officer for the Government of Malaysia` AND `the order is in operation`

-- Either route vests the property; both say "without any conveyance, assignment or transfer whatever".
GIVEN `in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `vested in the Chief Secretary immediately before 27 February 1959` IS A BOOLEAN, `vested under the 1955 Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a President's order covers it` IS A BOOLEAN, `held by an officer for the Government of Malaysia` IS A BOOLEAN, `the order is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property is the Corporation's under s 7` IF
        `the property vested on 27 February 1959` `in Singapore` `vested in the Chief Secretary immediately before 27 February 1959` `vested under the 1955 Ordinance`
    OR  `the property vests by President's order` `a President's order covers it` `held by an officer for the Government of Malaysia` `the order is in operation`

§§ `8 -- rights, powers and liabilities of the Chief Secretary`

-- s 8: "All rights, powers and liabilities which were, immediately before 27 February 1959, vested in or imposed on the Chief
-- Secretary, Federation of Malaya, by virtue of the [1955 Ordinance] or otherwise shall, on that date, be vested in or be imposed on
-- the Corporation."
--
-- "or otherwise": unlike property under s 7(1), a right or liability passes whatever its source, and s 8 carries no "in Singapore"
-- limit.
GIVEN `held by the Chief Secretary immediately before 27 February 1959` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the right or liability passed to the Corporation` IF
    `held by the Chief Secretary immediately before 27 February 1959`

§§ `9 -- the Corporation under the Land Acquisition Act 1966`

-- s 9: "For the purposes of the Land Acquisition Act 1966, the Corporation shall be deemed to be a company, and any person duly
-- appointed by the Corporation and authorised by the Minister shall be deemed to be an officer of the company."
GIVEN `appointed by the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is deemed an officer of the company` IF
    `appointed by the Corporation` AND `authorised by the Minister`

§§ `11 -- saving`

-- s 11: "Nothing in this Act shall affect the rights of the Government or of any bodies politic or corporate or other persons except
-- such as are mentioned in this Act and those claiming by, from or under them."
GIVEN `mentioned in this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from or under someone mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act may affect the person's rights` IF
    `mentioned in this Act` OR `claims by, from or under someone mentioned`
